WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.314
Step three reads the long-lived
credentials: one row per active access key,

2
00:00:05.314 --> 00:00:10.442
service-specific credential, API key,
auth token and customer secret key,

3
00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:14.288
with its age, its last use for
AWS keys, and its exception.

4
00:00:14.288 --> 00:00:17.276
Two are under exceptions until 2027:

5
00:00:17.276 --> 00:00:23.351
S V C dash app dash sync's access key and
H R dash report dash reader's API key.

6
00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:24.737
Look at the ages.

7
00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:29.574
S V C dash legacy dash F T P's key
is more than nine hundred days old,

8
00:00:29.574 --> 00:00:34.875
and was last used in December 2025, so
it's also a ninety-day unused lead.

9
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:38.167
H R dash build dash push's
auth token is five hundred

10
00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:41.537
and eighty-two days old, and
auth tokens never expire.

11
00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:45.050
The file holds identifiers
only, never a secret.
